      "name": "Foo definition",
      "description": "A Foo is an arrangement of wooden objects. A Foo has a single wooden brick which supports two wooden blocks that do not touch each other. The two blocks, which can be bricks or cylinders, both support a single wooden brick that sit on top of them.",
      "equivalentTo": "Foo = {base: brick, supports: [block1, block2], top: brick} where supports(base, block1) AND supports(base, block2) AND supports(block1, top) AND supports(block2, top) AND NOT touches(block1, block2)"
